On the Zaurus I usually play Nethack(-qt) with partial menus, for the
convenience of working with the stylus. But earlier tonight, I'd found a
lucky temple of Huan Ti after going through the mines, sokoban, and a
treasure zoo. This looked like a great chance to get an armor blessing and
make up for the boulders I had to smash after a stone giant threw one into
my path. So into the bag I went, and then it became "How on earth do I
split up this 13000 gold?" I tried all kinds of keyboard tricks and
failed, and was about to plead for help in the group, when I realized that
playing with the menustyle option might be what I needed. Sure enough, I
was able to take an arbitrary amount by using the traditional menus.

So my question is, why was the traditional menu the only means that worked
for me, and are there some keyboard modifiers or other shortcuts I can use
when dropping/picking ip things on the floor, or inserting/removing items
in containers, so I can take an arbitrary quantity?



